      "colour_group": "sport",
      "mix_tags": "lint-magnet",
      "notes": "Inside out, dig? Never no softener — it films right over them fibers that do all the wickin' and stretchin'. A cup o' white vinegar in the rinse resets a load that's already gone funky. Covers tops, shorts, and base layers, Jack — one fabric family, one wash. Mixed colors are cool in one run: at 30 °C them polyester dyes barely budge. 'Cept a brand-new black or hot red piece, which can bleed color for a wash or two — give that one its own solo run first, solid.",
      "reference_name": "",
      "reference_link": ""
